const e="rockhampton-dance-festival",d=2026,o="Read the whole 2026 Preliminary Program (cover and fees, Code of Conduct, 45 General Rules, 12 Dance Rules, the awards and bursaries list, and all section listings). Placed: general rules, eligibility, registration and music upload, fees, dates, venue and backstage rules, marks and aggregates, prizes, group rules, conduct, judging, protests. Section listings (which age sections each style runs, section numbers, time limits) are in the competition rows. The template merges the solo, duo/trio and group sections of one style into one item, so each row names every section of that style. Trophy and award names are kept without the names of donors and winners; every section also has its own named trophy, not listed here. Edition facts are Variables: dates, closing dates, age date, trophy return date and places, venue, adjudicator (printed as 'To be advised'), website, enquiries email, seven fees, administration fee, Elite prize. Printed twice with different wording: the cover says no late entries will be accepted, and General Rule 2 says late entries may be accepted at the committee's choice at double fees. The program does not say which is newer, so the cover wording is written and Rule 2 is recorded here. Trophy holding is printed as nine months (General Rule 26) and as eight months per year when a Solo Aggregate is tied; both are written as printed. Rule 33 refers to 'Rule 42' for curtain approval, but the curtain rules are Rules 32 and 33 (a numbering slip in the program). Not printed: the venue street address, any second venue, the adjudicator, ticket prices, the daily schedule, Group Weekend dates, time limits for Improvisations, Championships and the Elite Dancer Award, ages for the School Group sections, judging criteria or mark bands, and points for solo placings. The Group aggregate gives 1 point to a group with no place; the template carries First to Third and Highly Commended points only. The program labels the Elite sections 132 and 133 and prints no sections 129 to 131. Fee amounts carry a dollar sign only, no country code.",n=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Rockhampton Dance Festival, {{EventDates}}. Read these rules before you enter.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Entries for groups close on {{GroupClosingDate}}. All other entries close on {{OtherClosingDate}}. Entries close sooner if the festival reaches capacity. No late entries will be accepted. Age is counted as at {{AgeCutoffDate}}. All entries and payments are online. No cash payments are accepted.","Notes":["Entries: {{EntriesWebsite}}. Enquiries: {{EnquiriesContact}}.","The adjudicator is {{Adjudicator}}.","This is the preliminary program. Dates are subject to change with the number of entries.","Music must be uploaded no later than ten days before the festival starts.","All trophies must be returned by {{TrophyReturnDate}} to {{TrophyReturnPoints}}."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The rules are here for safety and to make sure the competition is fair and reasonable. Competitors, teachers, parents and friends must keep to them so the festival runs smoothly and in a friendly way.","All entry forms are part of the rules and regulations of the festival. By submitting an entry, participants agree to follow all festival rules, including the Code of Conduct.","Breaking any of the rules of competition will result in disqualification.","The Festival Management Committee may reject any entry.","Solo dance items are open sections for the 2026 festival.","The festival has Solos, Improvisations, Student Choreography, Championships, the Elite Dancer Award, Duos/Trios and Groups.","All choreography must be original. Any breach of copyright will result in immediate disqualification.","Strict time limits apply to all sections. They include entry and exit music (tags).","Open Solo, Duo and Trio: 3 minutes, for all dance styles except Musical Theatre/Novelty, Song and Dance and Demi-Character.","Open Solo, Duo and Trio for Musical Theatre/Novelty, Song and Dance and Demi-Character only: 3 minutes 30 seconds.","Student Choreography: 2 minutes. Group sections: 5 minutes.","The Official Festival Program is emailed to entrants once it is final.","The order of appearance is chosen at random by the CompsOnline system and is printed in the Official Festival Program. Competitor numbers in the program are in sequence, as the CompsOnline and Music Uploads systems require.","Unless the Festival Secretary has approved other arrangements in advance, competitors must be ready to perform quickly when their number is called.","Competitors must check in before their section is announced. A competitor who is not present when called is a Withdrawal and may not be allowed to perform.","If a competitor leaves the stage and the performance is not complete, because of emotional distress or forgetting the routine, the competitor may, at the Adjudicator's choice, be invited to perform once only after the last competitor in the section. That competitor is not eligible for a placing. Technical problems are not penalised.","The committee may cancel or combine sections where there are not enough entries. This rule will be strictly enforced.","The committee may divide sections with a large number of competitors. Each split section is judged separately and a trophy is given to the competitor with the highest mark in each split section.","Sections are split as follows: 12 Years and Under at 15 competitors, divided by year of birth. 13 Years and Over at 20 competitors, divided by year of birth.","The Festival Management Committee has full control of the competition. It may change or reschedule the program when it decides this is best for the festival. All decisions of the committee are final.","The committee may correct any errors or omissions in the festival schedule and program.","The festival cannot promise special scheduling for travel or out-of-town plans, religious reasons, or conflicting competitions or personal plans. Requests for exceptional cases may be considered by the committee (see How to Register).","Studio logos are not allowed on costumes in Improvisation, Solo, Duo, Trio and Group sections. Failure to follow this may lead to penalties or disqualification, at the choice of the Adjudicator or the committee.","By entering, competitors (and their parents or guardians where it applies) allow the competitor to be interviewed, photographed or filmed during the festival. The festival may use this material for promotion, advertising and marketing without payment."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Competitors must meet the age limits as at {{AgeCutoffDate}}.","Proof of age may be required. Prizes are held back until it is given.","The competition is open to amateurs only. The Rockhampton Dance Festival Committee defines who is an amateur and has the final decision on a competitor's status.","Solo dance items are open sections. There is no restricted or pre-open level in the solo sections.","Competitors must compete under their own name.","Duo and Trio entries must list all competitors at the time of entry.","Dancers may not dance up into an older Open Solo age section. Exception: a dancer who is eligible for Tiny Tots 4 Years and Under may choose either Tiny Tots 4 Years and Under or the Open Classical Ballet 5 and 6 Years solo, but not both.","A dancer who is eligible for the Tiny Tot Improvisation section (6 Years and Under) may not dance up into any other Improvisation section.","In Duo and Trio sections, a competitor may choose to compete in an older age group. That competitor may then not compete in the own-age Duo or Trio sections of the same dance style.","In Group sections, a competitor may choose to compete in the own age group, an older age group, or both.","Competitors in the Adult Group (Any Dance) section must be 18 years or older as at {{AgeCutoffDate}}.","A competitor must not perform the same item more than once at any one festival. The exception is Championship events, for 2026 only.","Relatives of the Adjudicator are not eligible to enter the festival.","Parents, guardians, teachers and competitors must not have communicated with, taken lessons from, or had any professional or personal dealings with the Adjudicator or the Adjudicator's school in the six months before, or during, the festival. This includes all forms of communication, including social media. The committee may disqualify a competitor if this rule is broken by the competitor or by a parent, guardian or teacher.","To enter a Championship section, a competitor must meet the requirements printed in the rules of that Championship.","To enter the Elite Dancer Award, a competitor must meet the requirements printed in the rules of that award."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["All entries must be submitted online at {{EntriesWebsite}}. The entrant is fully responsible for the accuracy of the entry.","Entries for groups close on {{GroupClosingDate}}. All other entries close on {{OtherClosingDate}}.","Entries close sooner if the festival reaches capacity. If sections fill before the closing dates, the entries that are finished and paid will be accepted.","No late entries will be accepted.","Entry fees must be paid by the closing date to make the entry valid.","All payments are made online. No cash payments are accepted.","Programs can also be ordered through the festival website. They are emailed when finished.","All music for the festival must be uploaded online through the Music Uploads system. Instructions are given to competitors.","Music must be uploaded no later than ten days before the festival starts. Music files must be in MP3 format.","The competitor alone is responsible for uploading the correct, complete and playable music file for each routine.","If a music file is damaged, incomplete or cannot be played, the festival may try to tell the competitor before the festival. The festival cannot repair or edit music files and accepts no responsibility for music faults.","If music is not uploaded by the deadline, the entry is treated as withdrawn and the entry fee is not refunded.","For Demi-Character and National sections, the name of the Demi-Character or National dance must be entered in the right field during the music upload.","Requests for special scheduling in exceptional cases must be in writing and come with a non-refundable administration fee of {{ProgrammingRequestFee}}. Paying the fee does not promise approval. All decisions of the committee are final.","Group sections: curtain use must be requested through Music Uploads, stating which group section needs it. The studio teacher may also send a written form or email with curtain needs to the Festival Secretary for committee approval before the festival starts.","Groups: only one helper per group may be backstage. If more are needed, written permission must be asked from the committee and sent with the entry.","A competitor who must move behind the stage back curtain during an item must send written notice with the entry.","Enquiries: {{EnquiriesContact}}."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees","Items":["Improvisation items: {{ImprovisationFee}}.","Student Choreography items: {{StudentChoreographyFee}}.","Solo items: {{SoloFee}}.","Duo/Trio items: {{DuoTrioFee}}.","Group items: {{GroupFee}}.","Championships: {{ChampionshipFee}}.","Elite Solo item: {{EliteFee}}.","Entry fees include cover under the APRA AMCOS, ARIA and PPCA blanket licences, which allow copyright music and sound recordings to be used at the festival.","A request for special scheduling needs a non-refundable administration fee of {{ProgrammingRequestFee}}.","If the festival is cancelled because of catastrophic or unforeseen events, refunds follow CompsOnline policy, less any online booking fees and PayPal or credit card fees.","The committee may withdraw and refund Group entries if it must, because of timing. Any such decision is told to the entrant as soon as possible after entries close.","Entry to the auditorium needs a bought ticket. The ticket price is not printed in the program."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates and Program","Items":["The festival is on {{EventDates}}.","Entries for groups close on {{GroupClosingDate}}. All other entries close on {{OtherClosingDate}}.","Music must be uploaded no later than ten days before the festival starts.","All trophies must be returned by {{TrophyReturnDate}}.","The program has Group Weekends. The dates of each section are in the Official Festival Program, which is emailed once it is final.","Dates are subject to change with the number of entries. The committee may change or reschedule the program."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue and Backstage Rules","Items":["The festival is held at {{Venue}}.","Employees of the hired venue must be obeyed at all times in the venue. During the festival they are designated officials.","Information on dressing room allocation is given closer to the festival. Where possible, during Group Weekends, competitors must arrive dressed at the Pilbeam Theatre.","Parents and guardians may go backstage during Group Weekends up to 15 minutes before each session begins, unless the committee has approved it earlier (for example to help with props).","Competitors must not stay in dressing rooms after their section and must leave quickly.","Dressing rooms are given to dance studios and change each year, with group numbers and needs in mind.","For Solo, Duo and Trio competitors, one accompanying person per performer may be in the dressing room areas.","Extended family members must wait away from dressing rooms, green rooms and backstage areas. Prams are not allowed in backstage or dressing room areas at any time.","Failing to follow these rules may lead to limited access, as decided by festival staff or the Executive Committee.","For competitors 8 Years and Under in Solo, Duo and Trio sections, one parent or guardian may go with the competitor backstage or side-stage to help with props or to support the competitor before the performance. Only competitors performing in the current section may be side-stage.","Competitors may not rehearse at any festival venue once the festival has begun, including on stage, in bar areas or in any restricted public or backstage space, unless the Executive Committee has approved it. Marking a routine with earphones is allowed outside the theatre and backstage areas if it does not block other venue users. This rule is strictly enforced and a breach may lead to disqualification.","Only one helper per group may be backstage. Written permission is needed for more. Extra helpers will be asked to leave backstage at once. Groups of 5 Years and Under and 7 Years and Under may need more help, but this must also be asked in writing.","Helpers may move props, set stage positions and keep passages clear for runners. No prompting is allowed side-stage. Group helpers must stay seated once the group performance has begun, unless the committee has approved otherwise in writing.","All 9 Years and Under, 7 Years and Under and 5 Years and Under groups must have a named chaperone. The names of all helpers and chaperones must be given together. Approved helpers and chaperones get a pass, which must be worn at all times backstage.","Not allowed on the stage and surrounding performance areas: glass, sand, water or liquids of any kind, creams, powders, fog, dry ice, food, and anything that may break apart on stage. Loose material, such as straw, must be fully held inside fine mesh.","Chalk, body paint, powder or any substance that may transfer to the stage floor is not allowed.","No open flames are allowed, including candles, sparklers, cigarettes and lighters.","No foreign substances may be left on stage when an item ends.","Footwear must stay fully covered until the competitor is ready to enter the side-stage area, to stop hair spray, glitter or chemicals reaching the stage floor.","Props must be kept to a minimum. They are limited to items that can be placed on stage within one minute. A competitor with one prop may ask the Convenor or Conductor to place it on stage. A Pilbeam Theatre technician may also help to place and remove props at any time.","All props must be taken backstage before the session (morning, afternoon or evening), during the set dock opening times, and collected straight after the session ends. The committee accepts no responsibility for props before, during or after performances. All props must follow the venue's workplace health and safety rules.","Curtain use is allowed in Group sections only. It is not allowed in any other section, whatever the props or stage position. In 2026 a festival backdrop is used and may not be changed.","Only authorised Pilbeam Theatre employees may operate the stage curtains (front and back), under workplace health and safety law. A Pilbeam Theatre technician is at every section where curtain use has been approved.","For safety, competitors should not run or walk behind the stage back-drop or back curtain. They must use the set passages. A competitor who moves behind the back curtain does so at their own risk.","No changes to the stage lighting are allowed during the festival.","Entry to the auditorium needs a bought ticket. This applies to everyone, including parents, family, teachers and competitors. No one may enter the auditorium without a valid ticket."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Marks, Placings and Aggregates","Items":["In each section, competitors are given marks out of 100. The placing is decided by the highest score.","In Championship sections, marks out of 100 are given for each item. The winner is the competitor with the highest combined score.","The Adjudicator decides whether marks are announced or released.","The Adjudicator may give shared placings where performances are judged to be of equal merit.","All groups are marked out of 100 by the Adjudicator. For the Group Aggregate Award, points are given as follows: a performing group with no place 1 point, Highly Commended 2 points, Third 3 points, Second 4 points, First 5 points. The group with the highest total points across all its performances wins.","Solo Aggregate Awards are decided by adding the points received in the sections listed for each award. If there is a tie, each winner receives the trophy for an equal time of eight months per year (for example, two winners hold it for four months each).","Ballet Aggregate, Junior (12 Years and Under) and Senior (13 Years and Over): Open Ballet Solo (no pointe), Open Demi-Character Solo and Open National Dance Solo.","Jazz Aggregate, Junior and Senior: Open Jazz Solo, Open Contemporary Solo, and one of Open Hip Hop Solo or Open Lyrical Solo. Points are counted from the highest three sections.","Tap Aggregate, Junior and Senior: Open Tap Solo, Open Waltz Tap Solo and Open Speed Tap Solo.","Most Versatile Dancer Aggregate (any age): the competitor must perform six Open Solo sections. Three are compulsory: Open Ballet Solo (no pointe), Open Jazz Solo and Open Tap Solo. The other three may be any of: Open Demi-Character, National Dance, Lyrical, Contemporary, Hip Hop, Acro, Waltz Tap, Speed Tap, Song and Dance, Cabaret/Broadway Jazz, Musical Theatre/Novelty or Neo-Classical Solo. Points are counted from all three compulsory sections plus the three highest-scoring other sections.","Musical Theatre Aggregate, Junior and Senior: Open Song and Dance Solo, Open Musical Theatre/Novelty Solo, and Open Cabaret/Broadway Jazz Solo (13 Years and Over only).","Improvisation Aggregate, Junior and Senior: the Adjudicator chooses the Most Outstanding Junior Improvisation and the Most Outstanding Senior Improvisation. For 2026 the Adjudicator makes this award instead of counting points, because the number of Improvisations is limited."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Awards and Prizes","Items":["Official certificates are given to all place-getters: First, Second, Third, Very Highly Commended and Highly Commended.","All competitors in these sections get a certificate: the 5 Years and Under Group sections, the 4 Years and Under Tiny Tots Solo, and the Tiny Tots Duo/Trio.","Every section has its own trophy. Perpetual trophies are held by winners for nine months and must then be returned to the festival.","Trophy holders must keep the trophy safe, return it at their own cost, and make sure it is cleaned and engraved before it is returned. The committee does not arrange or pay for engraving and does not accept responsibility for trophies once they are presented.","All trophies must be returned by {{TrophyReturnDate}} to {{TrophyReturnPoints}}.","No extra trophies, prizes or awards are accepted or added once the competition has begun.","Points awards (chosen by points received during the festival): Ballet Aggregate Award, Junior and Senior. Jazz Aggregate Award, Junior and Senior. Tap Aggregate Award, Junior and Senior. Musical Theatre Aggregate, Junior and Senior. Most Versatile Dancer Bursary. Highest Points in Any Group, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Group Aggregate Award. Improvisation Aggregate Award, Junior and Senior.","Adjudicator's awards (chosen by the Adjudicator): Encouragement Awards for Ballet, Jazz, Tap, Contemporary, Lyrical and Musical Theatre, each for Junior and Senior.","Adjudicator's awards: Most Promising Performer in Tiny Tots. Most Promising Performer in Ballet, Jazz, Tap, Contemporary, Lyrical and Musical Theatre, each for Junior and Senior.","Adjudicator's awards: Most Outstanding Duo/Trio Item. Most Outstanding Student Choreography Award. Most Outstanding Male Dancer. Most Outstanding Female Dancer. Festival Adjudicators Award.","Adjudicator's awards: Bursary for the Elite Dancer, Junior and Senior. Bursary Encouragement Award for any Open section. Sportsmanship Award. Festival Encouragement Award for all ages. President Award.","Championship sections give a Winner trophy and a Runner Up trophy in the Junior and Senior divisions.","Elite Dancer Award winners (one in each of the Junior and Senior sections) receive a trophy, a prize pack and {{ElitePrize}}."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Duo, Trio and Group Rules","Items":["A Group must have four or more competitors.","For the 2026 festival, competitors may dance with more than one group in a section.","No extra time is given for costume, hair or make-up changes. Studios must plan entries carefully so that competitors are ready when called.","More than one group from the same dance studio may enter the same section. The committee may withdraw and refund entries if it must, because of timing. This is told to the entrant as soon as possible after entries close.","Group sections may use a curtain. Use must be requested through Music Uploads."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Code of Conduct and Behaviour","Items":["All contestants, parents and supporters must show good sportsmanship at all times. Unsportsmanlike behaviour may lead to disqualification or removal from the theatre property.","The committee has a zero-tolerance policy for unacceptable behaviour. This includes verbal abuse of any person, obscene or offensive language, loud, aggressive or disruptive behaviour, and inappropriate conduct on social media about the festival.","Committee members and designated officials may give directions at any time to keep the festival running smoothly and efficiently. A person who refuses to follow a direction may be asked to leave the venue. Continued refusal may lead to further action, including calling the police.","If a child behaves in a way the committee or its representatives find unacceptable, the child may be removed from the venue. If the child is a competitor, they may be disqualified from the current section and possibly from other sections.","Adults (audience, teachers, parents, guardians or volunteers) must behave in a way that supports a safe, fair and respectful festival. An adult whose behaviour is disruptive, aggressive, frightening or disrespectful to competitors, volunteers, adjudicators, staff or others may be asked to leave the venue.","If the adult is linked to a competitor, the competitor may be disqualified. This applies when the adult's behaviour affects the fairness of the competition, breaks the rules, or creates an unsafe or hostile place.","The committee may stop the adult, and any competitors the adult is responsible for, from taking part in more sections or future festivals. In cases of harassment, threats or safety concerns, the matter may be passed to the proper authorities.","An official is anyone the committee appoints to help run the festival, such as a marshal, a backstage worker or a door keeper.","All selections, costumes, props, backing music, choreography and dress must be suitable for children and suitable for family viewing. Children are in the audience at all times.","Costumes must not put a competitor at risk of showing themselves to the audience, on purpose or by accident. Tights must be worn under any costume that does not have a defined, sewn-in leg.","Choreography must be suitable for the age and must not include movements or gestures that could reasonably be seen as explicit, sexual or offensive.","Music must be suitable for the age and must not contain explicit or hidden sexual references, references to drugs or alcohol, or references to violence.","The Executive Committee may also decide whether costume, music and choreography are suitable for the family-friendly nature of the competition. All such decisions are final.","Photographic or recording devices of any kind are not allowed in the auditorium and side-stage areas. This includes video cameras, cameras, mobile phones, tablets and audio or video recorders. Official festival photographers and videographers are exempt.","Breaking the photography rule may lead to disqualification of the competitor, removal from the venue, or being reported to the authorities if the breach is serious.","Competitors and their families must not approach or communicate with the Adjudicator during the festival."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging","Items":["In each section competitors are given marks out of 100.","If the Adjudicator decides that any work or its presentation (including costume) is not suitable for family viewing, the Adjudicator may take off marks or refuse to mark the performance at all. The Adjudicator's decision is final.","Adjudication decisions must not be discussed with the Adjudicator.","An audio adjudication for each performance is given through the competitor's Music Uploads account. This does not include Improvisation sections.","If the Adjudicator cannot do the job because of unforeseen events, the committee may appoint a substitute Adjudicator.","Some festival committee members and volunteers may also be parents or teachers of competitors. They may need to speak to the Adjudicator only for festival business."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Protests and Objections","Items":["A protest or objection of a technical nature must be sent to the Festival Executive Committee, which decides it. Its decision is final and accepted without further appeal.","Complaints must be sent by email to the official festival email address.","A protest must be made in writing, given to the Secretary of the Festival Executive Committee, and sent within one hour after the end of the section in which the matter arose."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Rockhampton Dance Festival 2026 Preliminary Program (rules and all sections)","Url":"https://www.comps-online.com.au/Documents/Organiser/OR000005/EV004093/Rule/Preliminary%20Program%202026.pdf"}]}`),t=[],a=[],i=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Tiny Tots (Any Dance)","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Tiny Tots Solo (Any Dance) is Section 1, for 4 Years and Under. Time limit 3 minutes.","The Tiny Tots Duo/Trio (Any Dance) is Section 98, for 6 Years and Under. Time limit 3 minutes.","The Tiny Tots Group (Any Dance, excluding Ballet and Jazz) is Section 134, for 5 Years and Under. Time limit 5 minutes."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["A dancer who is eligible for the Tiny Tots 4 Years and Under solo may choose either this solo or the Open Classical Ballet 5 and 6 Years solo, but not both."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Tiny Tots Solo (Any Dance) is Section 1, for 4 Years and Under. Time limit 3 minutes.\\n- The Tiny Tots Duo/Trio (Any Dance) is Section 98, for 6 Years and Under. Time limit 3 minutes.\\n- The Tiny Tots Group (Any Dance, excluding Ballet and Jazz) is Section 134, for 5 Years and Under. Time limit 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A dancer who is eligible for the Tiny Tots 4 Years and Under solo may choose either this solo or the Open Classical Ballet 5 and 6 Years solo, but not both."},{"Title":"Classical Ballet","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Open Classical Ballet Solo (no pointe) is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 2 to 7.","The Classical Ballet Group is for 5 Years and Under, 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 136 to 140."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Open Classical Ballet Solo (no pointe) is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 2 to 7.\\n- The Classical Ballet Group is for 5 Years and Under, 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 136 to 140."},{"Title":"Classical Ballet Pointe","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Open Classical Ballet Pointe Solo is for 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 8 and 9."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Open Classical Ballet Pointe Solo is for 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 8 and 9."},{"Title":"Neo-Classical Ballet","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Neo-Classical: modern ballet-based choreography with clean lines. Pointe is allowed.","The Open Neo-Classical Ballet Solo is for 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 10 and 11."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Neo-Classical: modern ballet-based choreography with clean lines. Pointe is allowed.\\n- The Open Neo-Classical Ballet Solo is for 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 10 and 11."},{"Title":"National Dance","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["National Dance is traditional dance that shows cultural heritage. Scottish and Irish dancing are excluded.","The Open National Dance Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 12 to 17.","The National Dance Duo/Trio is for 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 103 to 105.","The National Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 141 to 143."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- National Dance is traditional dance that shows cultural heritage. Scottish and Irish dancing are excluded.\\n- The Open National Dance Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 12 to 17.\\n- The National Dance Duo/Trio is for 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 103 to 105.\\n- The National Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 141 to 143."},{"Title":"Demi-Character","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Demi-Character is classical-based dance with clear characterisation and an emotional storyline.","The Open Demi-Character Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 18 to 23."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Demi-Character is classical-based dance with clear characterisation and an emotional storyline.\\n- The Open Demi-Character Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 18 to 23."},{"Title":"Classical, Neo-Classical or Demi-Character Duo/Trio","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["One section for Classical Ballet, Neo-Classical or Demi-Character Duos/Trios. It is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 99 to 102.","Neo-Classical: modern ballet-based choreography with clean lines. Pointe is allowed.","Demi-Character: classical-based dance with clear characterisation and an emotional storyline."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- One section for Classical Ballet, Neo-Classical or Demi-Character Duos/Trios. It is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 99 to 102.\\n- Neo-Classical: modern ballet-based choreography with clean lines. Pointe is allowed.\\n- Demi-Character: classical-based dance with clear characterisation and an emotional storyline."},{"Title":"Song and Dance","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Open Song and Dance Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 24 to 29.","The Song and Dance Group is for 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 144 to 147."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Open Song and Dance Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 24 to 29.\\n- The Song and Dance Group is for 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 144 to 147."},{"Title":"Song and Dance, Cabaret or Novelty Duo/Trio","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["One section for Song and Dance, Cabaret or Novelty Duos/Trios. It is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 106 to 109."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- One section for Song and Dance, Cabaret or Novelty Duos/Trios. It is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 106 to 109."},{"Title":"Tap","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Open Tap Solo (traditional 4/4 rhythm) is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 30 to 35.","The Tap Duo/Trio is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 110 to 113.","The Tap Group is for 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 148 to 151."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Open Tap Solo (traditional 4/4 rhythm) is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 30 to 35.\\n- The Tap Duo/Trio is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 110 to 113.\\n- The Tap Group is for 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 148 to 151."},{"Title":"Waltz Tap","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Open Waltz Tap Solo (3/4 rhythm) is for 8 Years and Under, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 36 to 40."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Open Waltz Tap Solo (3/4 rhythm) is for 8 Years and Under, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 36 to 40."},{"Title":"Speed Tap","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Open Speed Tap Solo is for 8 Years and Under, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 41 to 45."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Open Speed Tap Solo is for 8 Years and Under, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 41 to 45."},{"Title":"Jazz","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Jazz is energetic dance that shows individual style, with leaps, turns and footwork.","The Open Jazz Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 46 to 51.","The Jazz Duo/Trio is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 114 to 117.","The Jazz Group is for 5 Years and Under, 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 152 to 156."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Jazz is energetic dance that shows individual style, with leaps, turns and footwork.\\n- The Open Jazz Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 46 to 51.\\n- The Jazz Duo/Trio is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 114 to 117.\\n- The Jazz Group is for 5 Years and Under, 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 152 to 156."},{"Title":"Hip Hop","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Hip Hop is energetic movement taken from break-dancing, with a focus on creativity and attitude.","The Open Hip Hop Solo is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 52 to 54.","The Hip Hop Duo/Trio is for 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 118 to 120.","The Hip Hop Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 157 to 159."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Hip Hop is energetic movement taken from break-dancing, with a focus on creativity and attitude.\\n- The Open Hip Hop Solo is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 52 to 54.\\n- The Hip Hop Duo/Trio is for 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 118 to 120.\\n- The Hip Hop Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 157 to 159."},{"Title":"Contemporary","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Contemporary is abstract, expressive theatrical dance that is not bound by classical ballet rules.","The Open Contemporary Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 55 to 60.","The Contemporary Duo/Trio is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 125 to 128.","The Contemporary Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 160 to 162."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Contemporary is abstract, expressive theatrical dance that is not bound by classical ballet rules.\\n- The Open Contemporary Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 55 to 60.\\n- The Contemporary Duo/Trio is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 125 to 128.\\n- The Contemporary Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 160 to 162."},{"Title":"Lyrical","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Lyrical is dance movement that is not held back by classical ballet and shows a flowing reading of the music.","The Open Lyrical Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 61 to 66.","The Lyrical Duo/Trio is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 121 to 124.","The Lyrical Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 163 to 165."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Lyrical is dance movement that is not held back by classical ballet and shows a flowing reading of the music.\\n- The Open Lyrical Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 61 to 66.\\n- The Lyrical Duo/Trio is for 8 Years and Under, 10 Years and Under, 14 Years and Under and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 121 to 124.\\n- The Lyrical Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 163 to 165."},{"Title":"Musical Theatre or Novelty","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Musical Theatre/Novelty: theatrical routines from stage or screen musicals. Singing or lip-syncing is allowed.","The Open Musical Theatre or Novelty Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 67 to 72."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Musical Theatre/Novelty: theatrical routines from stage or screen musicals. Singing or lip-syncing is allowed.\\n- The Open Musical Theatre or Novelty Solo is for 5 and 6 Years, 7 and 8 Years, 9 and 10 Years, 11 and 12 Years, 13 and 14 Years, and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes 30 seconds. Sections 67 to 72."},{"Title":"Acro","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Acro Dance is a mix of classical dance technique and acrobatic elements.","The Open Acro Solo is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 73 to 75.","The Acro Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 172 to 174."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Acro Dance is a mix of classical dance technique and acrobatic elements.\\n- The Open Acro Solo is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 73 to 75.\\n- The Acro Group is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 172 to 174."},{"Title":"Cabaret/Broadway Jazz","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Cabaret/Broadway Jazz is high-energy Broadway-style jazz.","The Open Cabaret/Broadway Jazz Solo is for 13 and 14 Years and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 76 and 77."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":["Heels are allowed from age 13 and over."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Cabaret/Broadway Jazz is high-energy Broadway-style jazz.\\n- The Open Cabaret/Broadway Jazz Solo is for 13 and 14 Years and 15 Years and Over. Time limit 3 minutes. Sections 76 and 77.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Heels are allowed from age 13 and over."},{"Title":"Cabaret/Novelty Group","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Cabaret/Novelty Group is for 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 166 to 169."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Cabaret/Novelty Group is for 7 Years and Under, 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes. Sections 166 to 169."},{"Title":"Adult Group (Any Dance)","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Adult Group (Restricted) (Any Dance) is Section 135, for 18 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Adult Group (Restricted) (Any Dance) is Section 135, for 18 Years and Over. Time limit 5 minutes."},{"Title":"School Group (Any Dance)","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The School Group (any dance) has two sections: Section 170 Primary School and Section 171 Secondary School. Time limit 5 minutes.","The program prints no ages for the Primary School and Secondary School sections."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The School Group (any dance) has two sections: Section 170 Primary School and Section 171 Secondary School. Time limit 5 minutes.\\n- The program prints no ages for the Primary School and Secondary School sections."},{"Title":"Tiny Tot Improvisation","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rules 9 and 10 and Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Tiny Tot Improvisation is Section 78, for 6 Years and Under. The program prints no time limit."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["A dancer who is eligible for this section may not dance up into any other Improvisation section.","Competitors must be in the waiting area before the section is announced. A competitor who checks in after the section is announced is disqualified.","Each competitor is given a number, supplied in the Competitor Pack. It must be pinned to a plain leotard and worn for the whole time of all Improvisation sections the competitor takes part in.","All Improvisation competitors must wear plain, basic, non-sequined costumes of non-reflective material, suitable for the style of dance.","The Adjudicator gives no audio adjudication for Improvisation sections."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Tiny Tot Improvisation is Section 78, for 6 Years and Under. The program prints no time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A dancer who is eligible for this section may not dance up into any other Improvisation section.\\n- Competitors must be in the waiting area before the section is announced. A competitor who checks in after the section is announced is disqualified.\\n- Each competitor is given a number, supplied in the Competitor Pack. It must be pinned to a plain leotard and worn for the whole time of all Improvisation sections the competitor takes part in.\\n- All Improvisation competitors must wear plain, basic, non-sequined costumes of non-reflective material, suitable for the style of dance.\\n- The Adjudicator gives no audio adjudication for Improvisation sections."},{"Title":"Jazz Improvisation","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rules 9 and 10 and Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Jazz Improvisation is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Sections 79 to 81. The program prints no time limit."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Competitors must be in the waiting area before the section is announced. A competitor who checks in after the section is announced is disqualified.","Each competitor is given a number, supplied in the Competitor Pack. It must be pinned to a plain leotard and worn for the whole time of all Improvisation sections the competitor takes part in.","All Improvisation competitors must wear plain, basic, non-sequined costumes of non-reflective material, suitable for the style of dance.","The Adjudicator gives no audio adjudication for Improvisation sections."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Jazz Improvisation is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Sections 79 to 81. The program prints no time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Competitors must be in the waiting area before the section is announced. A competitor who checks in after the section is announced is disqualified.\\n- Each competitor is given a number, supplied in the Competitor Pack. It must be pinned to a plain leotard and worn for the whole time of all Improvisation sections the competitor takes part in.\\n- All Improvisation competitors must wear plain, basic, non-sequined costumes of non-reflective material, suitable for the style of dance.\\n- The Adjudicator gives no audio adjudication for Improvisation sections."},{"Title":"Contemporary/Lyrical Improvisation","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rules 9 and 10 and Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Contemporary/Lyrical Improvisation is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Sections 82 to 84. The program prints no time limit."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Competitors must be in the waiting area before the section is announced. A competitor who checks in after the section is announced is disqualified.","Each competitor is given a number, supplied in the Competitor Pack. It must be pinned to a plain leotard and worn for the whole time of all Improvisation sections the competitor takes part in.","All Improvisation competitors must wear plain, basic, non-sequined costumes of non-reflective material, suitable for the style of dance.","The Adjudicator gives no audio adjudication for Improvisation sections."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Contemporary/Lyrical Improvisation is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Sections 82 to 84. The program prints no time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Competitors must be in the waiting area before the section is announced. A competitor who checks in after the section is announced is disqualified.\\n- Each competitor is given a number, supplied in the Competitor Pack. It must be pinned to a plain leotard and worn for the whole time of all Improvisation sections the competitor takes part in.\\n- All Improvisation competitors must wear plain, basic, non-sequined costumes of non-reflective material, suitable for the style of dance.\\n- The Adjudicator gives no audio adjudication for Improvisation sections."},{"Title":"Musical Theatre Improvisation","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rules 9 and 10 and Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Musical Theatre Improvisation is done with a prop. It is for 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Sections 85 and 86. The program prints no time limit."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Competitors must be in the waiting area before the section is announced. A competitor who checks in after the section is announced is disqualified.","Each competitor is given a number, supplied in the Competitor Pack. It must be pinned to a plain leotard and worn for the whole time of all Improvisation sections the competitor takes part in.","All Improvisation competitors must wear plain, basic, non-sequined costumes of non-reflective material, suitable for the style of dance.","The Adjudicator gives no audio adjudication for Improvisation sections."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Musical Theatre Improvisation is done with a prop. It is for 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Sections 85 and 86. The program prints no time limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Competitors must be in the waiting area before the section is announced. A competitor who checks in after the section is announced is disqualified.\\n- Each competitor is given a number, supplied in the Competitor Pack. It must be pinned to a plain leotard and worn for the whole time of all Improvisation sections the competitor takes part in.\\n- All Improvisation competitors must wear plain, basic, non-sequined costumes of non-reflective material, suitable for the style of dance.\\n- The Adjudicator gives no audio adjudication for Improvisation sections."},{"Title":"Student Choreography","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Student Choreography Solo is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 2 minutes. Sections 87 to 89."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Student Choreography Solo is for 9 Years and Under, 12 Years and Under and 13 Years and Over. Time limit 2 minutes. Sections 87 to 89."},{"Title":"Classical Ballet Championship","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rules 5 and Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Section 90 Junior, Section 91 Senior. This Championship is made of the Classical Ballet Solo and the Demi-Character Solo.","The Junior division is 12 Years and Under. The Senior division is 13 Years and Over.","The program prints no time limit for Championships."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["To enter, the competitor must have entered and performed in the Open Classical Ballet Solo OR the Open Classical Ballet Pointe Solo, AND in the Open Demi-Character Solo, during the current festival.","A competitor who does not meet the requirements cannot compete in the Championship.","The competitor performs two routines of contrasting nature. At least one routine must not have been performed before at this year's festival.","Championship events are an exception, for 2026 only, to the rule that an item is performed only once at a festival."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Marks out of 100 are given for each item. The winner is decided by the total combined score.","Each division has a Winner trophy and a Runner Up trophy."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Section 90 Junior, Section 91 Senior. This Championship is made of the Classical Ballet Solo and the Demi-Character Solo.\\n- The Junior division is 12 Years and Under. The Senior division is 13 Years and Over.\\n- The program prints no time limit for Championships.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- To enter, the competitor must have entered and performed in the Open Classical Ballet Solo OR the Open Classical Ballet Pointe Solo, AND in the Open Demi-Character Solo, during the current festival.\\n- A competitor who does not meet the requirements cannot compete in the Championship.\\n- The competitor performs two routines of contrasting nature. At least one routine must not have been performed before at this year's festival.\\n- Championship events are an exception, for 2026 only, to the rule that an item is performed only once at a festival.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Marks out of 100 are given for each item. The winner is decided by the total combined score.\\n- Each division has a Winner trophy and a Runner Up trophy."},{"Title":"Tap Championship","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rules 5 and Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Section 92 Junior, Section 93 Senior. This Championship is made of a Slow Tempo Tap Solo and a Speed/Fast Tempo Tap Solo.","The Junior division is 12 Years and Under. The Senior division is 13 Years and Over.","The program prints no time limit for Championships."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["To enter, the competitor must have entered and performed in the Open Tap Solo OR the Open Waltz Tap Solo, AND in the Open Speed Tap Solo, during the current festival.","A competitor who does not meet the requirements cannot compete in the Championship.","The competitor performs two routines of contrasting nature. At least one routine must not have been performed before at this year's festival.","Championship events are an exception, for 2026 only, to the rule that an item is performed only once at a festival."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Marks out of 100 are given for each item. The winner is decided by the total combined score.","Each division has a Winner trophy and a Runner Up trophy."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Section 92 Junior, Section 93 Senior. This Championship is made of a Slow Tempo Tap Solo and a Speed/Fast Tempo Tap Solo.\\n- The Junior division is 12 Years and Under. The Senior division is 13 Years and Over.\\n- The program prints no time limit for Championships.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- To enter, the competitor must have entered and performed in the Open Tap Solo OR the Open Waltz Tap Solo, AND in the Open Speed Tap Solo, during the current festival.\\n- A competitor who does not meet the requirements cannot compete in the Championship.\\n- The competitor performs two routines of contrasting nature. At least one routine must not have been performed before at this year's festival.\\n- Championship events are an exception, for 2026 only, to the rule that an item is performed only once at a festival.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Marks out of 100 are given for each item. The winner is decided by the total combined score.\\n- Each division has a Winner trophy and a Runner Up trophy."},{"Title":"Jazz Championship","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rules 5 and Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Section 94 Junior, Section 95 Senior. This Championship is made of a Slow Tempo Solo (for example Lyrical or Contemporary) and a Fast Tempo Solo (for example Jazz).","The Junior division is 12 Years and Under. The Senior division is 13 Years and Over.","The program prints no time limit for Championships."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["To enter, the competitor must have entered and performed in the Open Contemporary Solo OR the Open Lyrical Solo, AND in the Open Jazz Solo, during the current festival.","A competitor who does not meet the requirements cannot compete in the Championship.","The competitor performs two routines of contrasting nature. At least one routine must not have been performed before at this year's festival.","Championship events are an exception, for 2026 only, to the rule that an item is performed only once at a festival."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Marks out of 100 are given for each item. The winner is decided by the total combined score.","Each division has a Winner trophy and a Runner Up trophy."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Section 94 Junior, Section 95 Senior. This Championship is made of a Slow Tempo Solo (for example Lyrical or Contemporary) and a Fast Tempo Solo (for example Jazz).\\n- The Junior division is 12 Years and Under. The Senior division is 13 Years and Over.\\n- The program prints no time limit for Championships.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- To enter, the competitor must have entered and performed in the Open Contemporary Solo OR the Open Lyrical Solo, AND in the Open Jazz Solo, during the current festival.\\n- A competitor who does not meet the requirements cannot compete in the Championship.\\n- The competitor performs two routines of contrasting nature. At least one routine must not have been performed before at this year's festival.\\n- Championship events are an exception, for 2026 only, to the rule that an item is performed only once at a festival.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Marks out of 100 are given for each item. The winner is decided by the total combined score.\\n- Each division has a Winner trophy and a Runner Up trophy."},{"Title":"Entertainment Championship","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rules 5 and Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["Section 96 Junior, Section 97 Senior. This Championship is made of a Musical Theatre/Novelty Solo and one of a Song and Dance Solo, a Cabaret/Broadway Jazz Solo, an Acro Solo or a Hip Hop Solo.","The Junior division is 12 Years and Under. The Senior division is 13 Years and Over.","The program prints no time limit for Championships."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["To enter, the competitor must have entered and performed in the Open Musical Theatre/Novelty Solo AND in one of the Open Song and Dance Solo, Open Cabaret/Broadway Jazz Solo, Open Acro Solo or Open Hip Hop Solo, during the current festival.","A competitor who does not meet the requirements cannot compete in the Championship.","The competitor performs two routines of contrasting nature. At least one routine must not have been performed before at this year's festival.","Championship events are an exception, for 2026 only, to the rule that an item is performed only once at a festival."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Marks out of 100 are given for each item. The winner is decided by the total combined score.","Each division has a Winner trophy and a Runner Up trophy."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Section 96 Junior, Section 97 Senior. This Championship is made of a Musical Theatre/Novelty Solo and one of a Song and Dance Solo, a Cabaret/Broadway Jazz Solo, an Acro Solo or a Hip Hop Solo.\\n- The Junior division is 12 Years and Under. The Senior division is 13 Years and Over.\\n- The program prints no time limit for Championships.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- To enter, the competitor must have entered and performed in the Open Musical Theatre/Novelty Solo AND in one of the Open Song and Dance Solo, Open Cabaret/Broadway Jazz Solo, Open Acro Solo or Open Hip Hop Solo, during the current festival.\\n- A competitor who does not meet the requirements cannot compete in the Championship.\\n- The competitor performs two routines of contrasting nature. At least one routine must not have been performed before at this year's festival.\\n- Championship events are an exception, for 2026 only, to the rule that an item is performed only once at a festival.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Marks out of 100 are given for each item. The winner is decided by the total combined score.\\n- Each division has a Winner trophy and a Runner Up trophy."},{"Title":"Elite Dancer Award","Source":"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rules 6 and Competition Sections","Sections":{"About":["The Elite Dancer Award is offered in two sections: Section 132 Elite Dancer Junior (12 Years and Under) and Section 133 Elite Dancer Senior (13 Years and Over). The program prints no time limit.","Competitors enter in the same way as for a standard solo section."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The competitor must have entered and competed in at least three Solo sections and one Championship section (any one) during the current festival.","Competitors may perform any style of dance. This is an Open section, judged separately from all other sections. It does not count toward aggregates or any other festival award.","The routine must be unseen at this year's festival. A new routine is compulsory.","There is one award only for each section.","All decisions of the Adjudicator and the festival committee about eligibility, performance standards and awards are final."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Winners receive a trophy, a prize pack and {{ElitePrize}}."],"Notes":["Entry fee for the Elite Solo item: {{EliteFee}}."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Elite Dancer Award is offered in two sections: Section 132 Elite Dancer Junior (12 Years and Under) and Section 133 Elite Dancer Senior (13 Years and Over). The program prints no time limit.\\n- Competitors enter in the same way as for a standard solo section.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The competitor must have entered and competed in at least three Solo sections and one Championship section (any one) during the current festival.\\n- Competitors may perform any style of dance. This is an Open section, judged separately from all other sections. It does not count toward aggregates or any other festival award.\\n- The routine must be unseen at this year's festival. A new routine is compulsory.\\n- There is one award only for each section.\\n- All decisions of the Adjudicator and the festival committee about eligibility, performance standards and awards are final.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Winners receive a trophy, a prize pack and {{ElitePrize}}.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry fee for the Elite Solo item: {{EliteFee}}."}]`),r=[],s=[{Key:"EventDates",Kind:"text",Label:"Festival dates",Value:"18-25 September 2026",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program cover"},{Key:"GroupClosingDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Closing date for Group entries",Value:"2026-05-17",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 (Entries close: Groups - 17 May)"},{Key:"OtherClosingDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Closing date for all other entries",Value:"2026-06-06",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 (All other entries close: 6 June)"},{Key:"AgeCutoffDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date on which age is counted",Value:"2026-01-01",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program General Rule 4 Age Eligibility"},{Key:"TrophyReturnDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to return trophies",Value:"2026-08-01",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1"},{Key:"TrophyReturnPoints",Kind:"address",Label:"Where trophies are returned",Value:{Name:"Puls8 Studios, or Prima Donna",Address:"160 Denison Street (Puls8 Studios), or Cnr Dean & High Streets (Prima Donna)",City:"",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Event venue",Value:{Name:"Pilbeam Theatre",Address:"",City:"Rockhampton",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"2026 Preliminary Program General Rules 12, 17, 33 (the program prints no street address)"},{Key:"Adjudicator",Kind:"text",Label:"Adjudicator",Value:"To be advised",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program cover (Adjudicator: To Be Advised)"},{Key:"EntriesWebsite",Kind:"link",Label:"Entries website",Value:"www.rockhamptondancefestival.org.au",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 (ENTRIES)"},{Key:"EnquiriesContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Enquiries",Value:{Name:"Rockhampton Dance Festival",Role:"Enquiries",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"rockhamptondancefestival@hotmail.com"},Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 (ENQUIRIES)"},{Key:"ImprovisationFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee: Improvisation items",Value:"$5.00",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 Section Entry Fees"},{Key:"StudentChoreographyFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee: Student Choreography items",Value:"$10.00",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 Section Entry Fees"},{Key:"SoloFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee: Solo items",Value:"$15.00",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 Section Entry Fees"},{Key:"DuoTrioFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee: Duo/Trio items",Value:"$20.00",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 Section Entry Fees"},{Key:"GroupFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee: Group items",Value:"$35.00",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 Section Entry Fees"},{Key:"ChampionshipFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee: Championships",Value:"$30.00",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 Section Entry Fees"},{Key:"EliteFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee: Elite Solo item",Value:"$15.00",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program p.1 Section Entry Fees"},{Key:"ProgrammingRequestFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Administration fee for a special scheduling request",Value:"$10 (non-refundable)",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program General Rule 42"},{Key:"ElitePrize",Kind:"prize",Label:"Elite Dancer Award prize money",Value:"$150 prize money",Source:"2026 Preliminary Program Dance Rule 6 and Competition Sections (Sections 132, 133)"}],l=[{Claim:"All rules, fees, dates, sections, aggregates and awards are those of the Rockhampton Dance Festival 2026 Preliminary Program.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own program and rules",Source:"Rockhampton Dance Festival 2026 Preliminary Program (Comps-Online document EV004093)",Url:"https://www.comps-online.com.au/Documents/Organiser/OR000005/EV004093/Rule/Preliminary%20Program%202026.pdf"}],c={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:o,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:t,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{a as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,l as Evidence,o as Note,n as Page,t as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,d as Year,c as default};
